    "overviewDetail": "Puerto Rico has emerged as a compelling destination for businesses seeking access to the United States market while benefiting from a favorable tax environment. As a US territory, it operates under federal legal frameworks but maintains its own tax system, making it uniquely positioned for companies looking to optimize operations and costs. The island has a long-standing industrial base, particularly in pharmaceuticals, manufacturing, and medical devices, and is now expanding into technology and service exports.\n\nThe government actively promotes foreign investment through Act 60, which consolidates multiple incentive programs offering reduced corporate tax rates, exemptions on dividends, and attractive personal tax benefits. Puerto RicoΓÇÖs infrastructure includes modern ports, international airports, and a robust telecommunications network, supporting both physical and digital businesses.\n\nWith increasing interest from US mainland companies, digital entrepreneurs, and global investors, Puerto Rico is evolving into a hybrid hub combining US market credibility with offshore efficiency. Its regulatory alignment with US standards, combined with competitive incentives, makes it an appealing jurisdiction for startups, SMEs, and multinational corporations looking to expand strategically.\n",
